From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:23:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/apple-dart: Requalify only the changed DCP
 SID23 leaves

Until the IOMFB session is qualified, every message the host sends the
DCP first runs the full health check, and for SID23 that check walks
every leaf of the inherited tables: each nonzero leaf outside the DCP's
own reservations goes through region_intersects(), under the table lock
with interrupts off. On the J604 the loader leaves five foreign 32-MiB
slots, up to 10240 leaves, and the DCP's startup makes 317 callbacks,
each acknowledged by one such send while the firmware waits. IOMFB
startup takes 4.8-4.9 s at boot there, and the firmware log advances in
steps of about 12 ms, one per round trip; the internal panel's real KMS
device then arrives some 5 s after the boot splash and the disk password
prompt are already up on simpledrm.

apple_dart_dcp_leaf_safe() depends only on the leaf value and on inputs
fixed at admission (the consumer and reserved-memory snapshots, the
linear map and System RAM). Remember the value each foreign leaf had
when it last passed, and run the qualification again only for a leaf
whose value changed. Every leaf is still read on every call and any
unsafe leaf still fails the domain, as before; an unchanged leaf keeps
its earlier verdict. The inherited SID0 and SID16 tables already keep
their expected values this way.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp.h | 11 +++++++++++
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c     | 11 +++++++++--
 2 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp.h b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp.h
index 49ed48c2f3..95c703277b 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp.h
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart-dcp.h
@@ -22,6 +22,11 @@ struct apple_dart_dcp {
 	u64 *root;
 	u64 *table[DCP_DART_ENTRIES];
 	u64 *expected[DCP_DART_ENTRIES];
+	/* SID23 foreign leaves: the value each leaf had when it last passed
+	 * apple_dart_dcp_leaf_safe(). Firmware may rewrite them; only a
+	 * changed leaf needs the (fixed-input) qualification again.
+	 */
+	u64 *qualified[DCP_DART_ENTRIES];
 	u64 entry[DCP_DART_ENTRIES];
 	struct resource leaf_regions[64];
 	unsigned int nr_leaf_regions;
@@ -596,6 +601,10 @@ static int apple_dart_dcp_import(struct apple_dart *dart, unsigned int sid,
 			dcp->expected[i] = apple_dart_retained_alloc(dart, DCP_DART_PAGE);
 			if (!dcp->expected[i])
 				return -ENOMEM;
+		} else {
+			dcp->qualified[i] = apple_dart_retained_alloc(dart, DCP_DART_PAGE);
+			if (!dcp->qualified[i])
+				return -ENOMEM;
 		}
 		for (unsigned int j = 0; j < DCP_DART_ENTRIES; j++) {
 			u64 leaf = READ_ONCE(dcp->table[i][j]);
@@ -610,6 +619,8 @@ static int apple_dart_dcp_import(struct apple_dart *dart, unsigned int sid,
 					sid, i, j, leaf);
 			if (sid != 23)
 				dcp->expected[i][j] = leaf;
+			else
+				dcp->qualified[i][j] = leaf;
 		}
 	}
 	/* Refuse an unstable root instead of trying to repair it. */
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index e9929282d0..908f39d238 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -3270,11 +3270,18 @@ static int __apple_dart_dcp_check(struct device *dev)
 		 * their physical ownership too, not just known firmware segments.
 		 */
 		if (dcp->sid == 23 && test_bit(i, dcp->foreign) && dcp->table[i])
-			for (unsigned int j = 0; j < DCP_DART_ENTRIES; j++)
-				if (!apple_dart_dcp_leaf_safe(dcp, READ_ONCE(dcp->table[i][j]))) {
+			for (unsigned int j = 0; j < DCP_DART_ENTRIES; j++) {
+				u64 leaf = READ_ONCE(dcp->table[i][j]);
+
+				/* Same verdict as last time: the inputs are fixed at admission. */
+				if (leaf == dcp->qualified[i][j])
+					continue;
+				if (!apple_dart_dcp_leaf_safe(dcp, leaf)) {
 					drift = true;
 					break;
 				}
+				dcp->qualified[i][j] = leaf;
+			}
 		if (drift)
 			break;
 	}
